  small halos at z = 7 -- up to x1.32 at 1e9 and x1.22 at 1e10 Msun -- and leaves M >= 1e11 within 1.9%; reading B (the
  action's content) leaves every mass within 0.03%.  The knob-free ceiling: the eps each data point requires changes by <= 0.08%
  (T) / 0.01% (B); the sharp-edged top hat, the most the band-pass allows, by <= 12.6%.  The chain neither eases nor
  worsens the tension at the host masses the data need; where LCDM is pressed (published Labbe, 7 < z < 8.5, Salpeter: eps 1.27),
  so is the chain.
